Real-World DevOps Interview Questions

> CI/CD & Deployment Strategy

Q1. How do you design a CI/CD pipeline for a microservices-based application?

Expected answer focus:
	•	Git (Bitbucket/GitHub)
	•	Build → Test → Scan → Package → Deploy
	•	Blue-Green / Canary deployment
	•	Rollback strategy

Mention tools like Jenkins, GitHub Actions, ArgoCD, Helm.



Q2. How do you prevent a bad deployment from breaking production?

Interviewers want:
	•	Canary deployments
	•	Feature flags
	•	Health checks
	•	Automated rollback
	•	SLO/SLA monitoring

Q3. What is the difference between GitOps and CI/CD?

CI/CD                       GitOps

Push based              Pull based

Jenkins deploys       ArgoCD deploys

Less secure               More secure

Manual rollback          Git-based rollback



> Kubernetes (Must Know)

Q4. How does Kubernetes decide where to run a Pod?

They expect:
	•	Scheduler
	•	Node resources
	•	Taints & tolerations
	•	Node affinity
	•	Pod anti-affinity


Q5. What happens when a Pod crashes?

Answer should include:
	•	kubelet
	•	restartPolicy
	•	ReplicaSet
	•	Liveness probe
	•	Controller recreates Pod


Q6. How do you do zero-downtime deployment in Kubernetes?

Expected:
	•	Rolling update
	•	Readiness probe
	•	Service load balancing
	•	HPA (optional)


